# UI & Accessibility

## Accessibility (WCAG-oriented)
- Semantic HTML first (`button`, `a`, `label`, headings in order).
- Visible focus rings; never remove outline without a clear replacement.
- Color is not the only signal — pair with text/icon.
- Contrast: aim for WCAG AA (text vs background).
- Images: meaningful `alt`; decorative images `alt=""`.
- Forms: every input has a label; errors linked via `aria-describedby`.
- Keyboard: all interactive elements reachable and operable without a mouse.

## Interaction
- Touch targets ≥ 44×44px on mobile.
- Hover is enhancement only — don’t hide essential actions on touch devices.
- Loading: skeletons/spinners for waits > ~300ms; prevent double-submit.
- Empty states: explain + one clear next action.

## Layout & Visual
- Clear visual hierarchy (size, weight, space — not just color).
- Consistent spacing scale; align to a grid; avoid one-off magic margins.
- Prefer real content/imagery over generic stock or abstract filler.
- Motion: purposeful (entrance, hierarchy, feedback), short, and `prefers-reduced-motion` respected.

## Content UI
- Primary CTA: one per viewport/section when possible.
- Microcopy: short, action-oriented (“Réserver un appel”, not “Soumettre”).
- Don’t use cards unless they group an interaction; avoid decorative boxes.
